 r←extension ListUsageDataFiles folder;names;wholeYear;years;months
⍝ Returns the names of the usage data files with `extension` ('zip', 'csv' or '*' for both) in `folder`, without
⍝ the folder, newest first: by year and then by month, the file of a whole year before any file
⍝ of that year that ends with a month.
⍝ Only what `IsUsageDataFilename` accepts is listed: the folder also holds the application log
⍝ and its year-end backups, and none of that is for the outside world.
⍝ The sorting cannot be left to the file system: on Linux the files come in directory order.
 r←''
 names←{⊃,/1↓⎕NPARTS ⍵}¨F.ListFiles folder,'usage-data-*.',extension
 names←(IsUsageDataFilename¨names)/names
 :If 0<≢names
     wholeYear←1+≢Months                                    ⍝ Sorts above any month
     years←{⊃⊃(//)⎕VFI 4↑⍵}¨(≢'usage-data-')↓¨names
     months←wholeYear{'-'≠⊃⍵:⍺ ⋄ ⊃⊃(//)⎕VFI 2↑1↓⍵}¨(≢'usage-data-YYYY')↓¨names
     r←names[⍒years,[1.5]months]
 :EndIf
⍝Done
